    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> merchant state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a>, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magan">Magan</a> and the luxuries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>.</li><li>Its springs, harbour, stamp seals and weight standard made it the clearing house of Gulf trade around 2000–1750 BCE.</li><li>Later ruled by Kassite governors and then a tributary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, it vanished as a polity in the 6th century BCE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Sumerian myth described <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a> as a pure land without sickness or old age, where the gods settled the flood hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziusudra">Ziusudra</a> and gave him eternal life.</p></aside>
    </section>

